{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-14T23:49:22.138Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"8883d09363214115c628d33e","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/8","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-14T23:49:22.138Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"The final metadata policy reads classic protection and active rulesets independently. Every readable required context remains mandatory even in fallback; missing permission/not-found metadata adds the conservative all-head-runs rule without discarding known requirements. Tests proved the earlier implementation could ignore readable rulesets when classic protection was unavailable, and could hide a second-source authorization failure. Those regressions now pass along with the inverse partial-permission cases (5/5 targeted). This refines the prior note: supplemental permission gaps may use fallback only while retaining all known required-check constraints. Malformed metadata and non-permission API errors still fail closed. The complete closeout suite now has 64 cases."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-14T23:49:22.138Z"}],"before_hash":"15e098de09ff7218f4cf9273a4a6b6ed25becf52365c162693abe533c639027b","after_hash":"e8a875b1dcfeccdb02b077a091be9a20b557ee7373057fd578a99e0ee86b2496","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"4f14cf5a224f2ebd5db9d1dc346d8cecbb14260ac