{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T01:16:45.244Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0400d60929071b1beaa422c1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/13","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T01:16:45.243Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Orchestrator verification with real data (2026-10-15), on a scratch clone of the pm-jev tracker, installed from the packed tarball. The first implementation closed EVERY linked non-terminal item. A dry run over pm-jev PRs 1, 7 and 17 planned to close the pm-jev epic and four open follow-ups (live acceptance pending an API key, the deferred Rust client, and two audit follow-ups) that PR 1 only linked for context. Fixed: a link alone never closes an item. An item closes only when it is in_progress (claimed work) or its link follows a GitHub-style closing keyword (Closes, Fixes, Resolves, Delivers) on the same line, and it is neither an Epic nor the parent of a non-terminal child. Every refusal gets a skip row naming the rule. The same dry run now closes only pm-jev-2mg8 (delivered by PR 17). Apply in the scratch clone wrote a close reason containing only GitHub facts (PR, URL, merge commit, head, merge time, passing checks), and a second apply closed 0. New test 'a mention is not delivery: open follow-ups, epics and parents with active children are never closed' fails when the rules are removed (behavioural revert, 0 of 1 pass); test/closeout.test.ts passes 65 of 65."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T01:16:45.244Z"}],"before_hash":"b551c5a74210521f178003a8d84d46b42bb5f86764e72cbbd617337d15bd9fce","after_hash":"a3ebe32b04ef02a34bde73163befa61d5e396265c3e31f06203c113e2c19b777","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"8294db529a85fd9286e7f5c11b36b284d8d4b6383902c31c2a6413985f4947c4"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-15T02:17:59.088Z","author":"claude-hub","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"0400d60929071b1beaa422c1","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.300","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/14","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-15T02:17:59.088Z","author":"claude-hub","text":"Review round 2 (PR 124, CodeRabbit on bfaf0f2), fixed by the orchestrator. (1) Major: the closing keyword matched anywhere earlier on the line, so prose such as 'Not fixed here; see <link>' declared delivery. declaresDelivery now scans backwards from the link with plain string operations and accepts the keyword only when nothing but earlier links (markdown or bare), commas and 'and' sit between them; colons and emphasis around the keyword are allowed. The three reported lines and further edge cases are regression-tested. (2) since now stops paging once a row was last updated before the cutoff, because rows arrive newest-updated first and a merge never postdates the PR update. (3) The command handler maps closeout failures to CommandError (selector and repository errors give USAGE exit 2, everything else GENERIC_FAILURE exit 1), so the host no longer re-runs the handler and repeats GitHub reads or remaining closes. Behavioural revert proofs: each of the three changes, removed alone, fails its new test."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-15T02:17:59.088Z"}],"before_hash":"a3ebe32b04ef02a34bde73163befa61d5e396265c3e31f06203c113e2c19b777","after_hash":"f972904afcd64b9065da3a68b287ec8f4c0cb43ba054d902bf2087bcb7cdd16f","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"5348768072800fb4909543a1aad34b530cb2bad322577889555c26ee33565b75"}
